</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>74</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi><mo>,</mo></math> whereas for&nbsp;[Fe(H2O)6]<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Reason B:&nbsp;In both complexes, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi></math> is present in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> oxidation state.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ccc98d", "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is false but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is true</p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa56"}, {"id": "16fe74", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa57"}, {"id": "b9552e", "text": "Both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;are true but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NOT</mi></math>&nbsp;the correct explanation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa58"}, {"id": "5047c4", "text": "<p>Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are true and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa59"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa5a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8803"], "concepts": ["6117b608478ae845c43c6354"], "question": {"text": "The number of complexes from the following with no electrons in the \\(t_2\\) orbital is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\mathrm{TiCl}_4,\\left[\\mathrm{MnO}_4\\right]^{-},\\left[\\mathrm{FeO}_4\\right]^{2-},\\left[\\mathrm{FeCl}_4\\right]^{-},\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}_4\\right]^{2-}\\)"}, "options": [{"id": "6e920f", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa5b"}, {"id": "dc0a73", "text": "4", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa5c"}, {"id": "09a6c3", "text": "3", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa5d"}, {"id": "fd3bfb", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa5e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f912ee0e063d929fa5f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205bb"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f4b"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8eeb"], "question": {"text": "Match the LIST-I with LIST-II<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_